plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/swift/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint:127-144 (swift_scope build + swiftlint call)
Severity: MEDIUM. Category: option injection via file names -> file write outside the repo.
Tracked .swift paths from git ls-files reach `swiftlint lint` as positional args with no ./ prefix and no -- terminator. A path whose first component starts with -- parses as an option; SwiftLint 0.65.1 has --output <path> and --write-baseline <path>, and swift-argument-parser accepts --opt=value.
Exploit: a malicious repo commits directory `--output=` containing tmp/x.swift; git lists `--output=/tmp/x.swift`; the -f test passes (the file exists in the repo); every code:lint / pre-commit run writes SwiftLint's report to absolute /tmp/x.swift, overwriting any user-writable *.swift path. Reproduced locally (created /tmp/sl_pwned.swift).
Fix: prefix each path with ./ (swift_scope+=("./${swift_file}")) or put -- before the paths; same hardening for the swift format calls in code/format:111-119.
